(3178208, 445744, 61413, '<td valign="top">An interesting take on the subject. Well executed too; I like the way you have included the ridge of the kerb to provide context.<br/> <br/>The narrow DOF looks a little like it was post-processed in...</td>', 'An interesting take on the subject. Well executed too; I like the way you have included the ridge of the kerb to provide context. The narrow DOF looks a little like it was post-processed in...', '2007-01-03 21:35:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178238, 445673, 61413, '<td valign="top">Very effective.</td>', 'Very effective.', '2007-01-03 21:42:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178313, 445759, 61413, '<td valign="top">This is terrific. The blue of the residue on the sparkler is perfectly exposed, which would be no mean feat photographing a burning sparkler!<br/> <br/>And the spectrum of colours from the burn - white, yellow, orange, red. Perfect. The narrow-ish DOF creates a definite impression of the sparks coming towards the viewer, too.</td>', 'This is terrific. The blue of the residue on the sparkler is perfectly exposed, which would be no mean feat photographing a burning sparkler! And the spectrum of colours from the burn - white, yellow, orange, red. Perfect. The narrow-ish DOF creates a definite impression of the sparks coming towards the viewer, too.', '2007-01-03 22:06:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178336, 445148, 61413, '<td valign="top">Perfectly composed. Love the lens flare on each star-bust, and the use of mono.<br/> <br/>There''s a noticeable "lean in" on the castle, though; which I would have tried to fix. And maybe just a bit of USM on the castle.<br/> <br/>Nice shot, though.</td>', 'Perfectly composed. Love the lens flare on each star-bust, and the use of mono. There''s a noticeable "lean in" on the castle, though; which I would have tried to fix. And maybe just a bit of USM on the castle. Nice shot, though.', '2007-01-03 22:12:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178368, 446122, 61413, '<td valign="top">Nice idea. Hope you didn''t start a bush-fire :-)</td>', 'Nice idea. Hope you didn''t start a bush-fire :-)', '2007-01-03 22:20:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178379, 446096, 61413, '<td valign="top">Very funny. And well composed. Love the lighting.</td>', 'Very funny. And well composed. Love the lighting.', '2007-01-03 22:23:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178388, 445792, 61413, '<td valign="top">Stunning. Loving the peak of clear sky and stars, and the texture and lighting of the clouds. The contrast of the orange glow with the dark blues of the sky is quite hypnotic.<br/> <br/>A shame about the pink-ish streak across the clouds. Would have been a 10 if not for that. But oh so close...</td>', 'Stunning. Loving the peak of clear sky and stars, and the texture and lighting of the clouds. The contrast of the orange glow with the dark blues of the sky is quite hypnotic. A shame about the pink-ish streak across the clouds. Would have been a 10 if not for that. But oh so close...', '2007-01-03 22:27:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178390, 444804, 61413, '<td valign="top">A bit over-enhanced for my tastes.</td>', 'A bit over-enhanced for my tastes.', '2007-01-03 22:28:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178393, 446033, 61413, '<td valign="top">Nicely done.</td>', 'Nicely done.', '2007-01-03 22:30:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178409, 445891, 61413, '<td valign="top">A completely different take on "fire works". Imaginative.<br/> <br/>The overall effect works well. I am distracted, though, by whatever it is intruding in silhouette on the left side of the ember. And by the hard lower edge of the whisp of smoke off to the right. But that''s me being picky - still a pleasing overall effect.</td>', 'A completely different take on "fire works". Imaginative. The overall effect works well. I am distracted, though, by whatever it is intruding in silhouette on the left side of the ember. And by the hard lower edge of the whisp of smoke off to the right. But that''s me being picky - still a pleasing overall effect.', '2007-01-03 22:37:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178418, 445363, 61413, '<td valign="top">Nice.<br/> <br/>It''s a shame that the top of the firework''s starburst is clipped off at the top. but apart from that it''s well composed. Love the whisp of green smoke, and the way the stars are still visible.</td>', 'Nice. It''s a shame that the top of the firework''s starburst is clipped off at the top. but apart from that it''s well composed. Love the whisp of green smoke, and the way the stars are still visible.', '2007-01-03 22:40:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178441, 444899, 61413, '<td valign="top">You''ve brough out some intriguing colours here. And well framed, too; I like the use of space on the left.<br/> <br/>I would have been tempted to try framing the combustion point on the sparkler a little lower - the stem of the sparkler looks a bit incongruous. Not sure if doing so would have made it any better though, I''d have to try and see.</td>', 'You''ve brough out some intriguing colours here. And well framed, too; I like the use of space on the left. I would have been tempted to try framing the combustion point on the sparkler a little lower - the stem of the sparkler looks a bit incongruous. Not sure if doing so would have made it any better though, I''d have to try and see.', '2007-01-03 22:48:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178456, 445682, 61413, '<td valign="top">The exaggerated "lean in" works well here, as does the softening effect of the smoke haze. Like the motion blur of the characters in the foreground.<br/> <br/>Mono was a good choice. All round fine pic!</td>', 'The exaggerated "lean in" works well here, as does the softening effect of the smoke haze. Like the motion blur of the characters in the foreground. Mono was a good choice. All round fine pic!', '2007-01-03 22:50:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178465, 445183, 61413, '<td valign="top">Nice composition, and restrained use of colour. Setting the black level high enough to eliminate any detail other than sources of light works well. And I like the way you''ve matched the frame with the colour of the star bursts - nice touch.</td>', 'Nice composition, and restrained use of colour. Setting the black level high enough to eliminate any detail other than sources of light works well. And I like the way you''ve matched the frame with the colour of the star bursts - nice touch.', '2007-01-03 22:52:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178471, 445644, 61413, '<td valign="top">Not sure I get the firework connection here...</td>', 'Not sure I get the firework connection here...', '2007-01-03 22:53:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178491, 445796, 61413, '<td valign="top">An extra point for having something other than a firework as the main subject, but still staying on topic :-)</td>', 'An extra point for having something other than a firework as the main subject, but still staying on topic :-)', '2007-01-03 22:57:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178493, 446084, 61413, '<td valign="top">A neat idea, well executed.<br/> <br/>The "ghosting" of the human subject as he positions himself behind each letter could have worked really well. It''s a shame the ghosts are so faint behind most of them, and so solid behind the "T".<br/> <br/>Did you think about trying to darken the grass, at all?</td>', 'A neat idea, well executed. The "ghosting" of the human subject as he positions himself behind each letter could have worked really well. It''s a shame the ghosts are so faint behind most of them, and so solid behind the "T". Did you think about trying to darken the grass, at all?', '2007-01-03 22:57:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178496, 445280, 61413, '<td valign="top">Nice.<br/> <br/>This is crying out for the "law of thirds" to be applied - re-cropping to place the towerover to the left. The spread of the fireworks would have supported this beautifully. And it could have used just a tiny bit of straightening.<br/> <br/>I can''t make up my mind whether the ANZ building in the bottom right is a distraction or not. It would be hard to crop it out without losing too many useful elements, though.<br/> <br/>Where was this taken from? I can''t think of any building from where you could have taken a shot this high. It looks like Nortcote Point in the background, so maybe somewhere around Albert Park?</td>', 'Nice. This is crying out for the "law of thirds" to be applied - re-cropping to place the towerover to the left. The spread of the fireworks would have supported this beautifully. And it could have used just a tiny bit of straightening. I can''t make up my mind whether the ANZ building in the bottom right is a distraction or not. It would be hard to crop it out without losing too many useful elements, though. Where was this taken from? I can''t think of any building from where you could have taken a shot this high. It looks like Nortcote Point in the background, so maybe somewhere around Albert Park?', '2007-01-03 22:57:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178497, 446094, 61413, '<td valign="top">This is a great idea. It''s a shame that the refraction through the glass didn''t work better.</td>', 'This is a great idea. It''s a shame that the refraction through the glass didn''t work better.', '2007-01-03 22:57:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178500, 445333, 61413, '<td valign="top">Well executed. But the different elements of the photo seem a bit incongruous, they don''t quite come together somehow.<br/> <br/>I suspect it would have been a better photo either without the firework (though not for this challenge, obviously) or without the car-light trails.<br/> <br/>Loving the colour and texture of the sand, though.</td>', 'Well executed. But the different elements of the photo seem a bit incongruous, they don''t quite come together somehow. I suspect it would have been a better photo either without the firework (though not for this challenge, obviously) or without the car-light trails. Loving the colour and texture of the sand, though.', '2007-01-03 22:58:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178502, 445443, 61413, '<td valign="top">The elements supporting the starburst really make this shot. The people silhouetted by the fire, the reflection. Nice.</td>', 'The elements supporting the starburst really make this shot. The people silhouetted by the fire, the reflection. Nice.', '2007-01-03 22:59:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178503, 445661, 61413, '<td valign="top">One of the better "firework landscape" shots in this challenge. The smoke haze caught in the street lights works well, as do the whisp of cloud and headlight trails.<br/> <br/>Looking forward to seeing how long you exposed this for :-)</td>', 'One of the better "firework landscape" shots in this challenge. The smoke haze caught in the street lights works well, as do the whisp of cloud and headlight trails. Looking forward to seeing how long you exposed this for :-)', '2007-01-03 22:59:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178506, 444918, 61413, '<td valign="top">Nice idea. Would''ve worked better if you''d managed to get some refraction happening through the glass capturing some detail of the starburst behind.</td>', 'Nice idea. Would''ve worked better if you''d managed to get some refraction happening through the glass capturing some detail of the starburst behind.', '2007-01-03 22:59:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178517, 445849, 61413, '<td valign="top">Reversing the image is a pretty neat idea!</td>', 'Reversing the image is a pretty neat idea!', '2007-01-03 23:00:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178551, 445420, 61413, '<td valign="top">Wow!<br/> <br/>I was beginning to get a bit jaded by all the pedestrian "here''s a picture of a firework" shots, and as this one started to unroll on my screen I thought I was going to get yet another one. But no!<br/> <br/>Love the framing, and the pervasiveness of the red hue. And the way the column of smoke discreetly merges into the general cloud cover. And the lighting of the house. And the sky pattersn. And the reflections. And the law of thirds applied in both dimensions. And, and, and...</td>', 'Wow! I was beginning to get a bit jaded by all the pedestrian "here''s a picture of a firework" shots, and as this one started to unroll on my screen I thought I was going to get yet another one. But no! Love the framing, and the pervasiveness of the red hue. And the way the column of smoke discreetly merges into the general cloud cover. And the lighting of the house. And the sky pattersn. And the reflections. And the law of thirds applied in both dimensions. And, and, and...', '2007-01-03 23:07:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(3178675, 446002, 62727, '<td valign="top">ROFLOL!!!</td>', 'ROFLOL!!!', '2007-01-03 23:41:54.000000', NULL, 1),
