(3199493, 445420, 30861, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pineapple:</b></div><hr/><i> Well done.  On the top right hand corner, what are those striations? or is it my streaky monitor? ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It''s an artifact that shows up when extreme shadow recovery via tone mapping is combined with heavy Neat Image, I think. Without the NI the darkest sky was extremely grainy; with it, the striations creep in. I didn''t have time to figure out a work-around. It''s not the first time I have seen it, incidentally.</td>', 'Originally posted by pineapple: Well done.  On the top right hand corner, what are those striations? or is it my streaky monitor? ;-)   It''s an artifact that shows up when extreme shadow recovery via tone mapping is combined with heavy Neat Image, I think. Without the NI the darkest sky was extremely grainy; with it, the striations creep in. I didn''t have time to figure out a work-around. It''s not the first time I have seen it, incidentally.', '2007-01-09 10:09:53.000000', NULL, 0),
